  "verbalization": "Tranilast, through its indication for Vasomotor Rhinitis and Allergic Rhinitis, is linked to Fluticasone Furoate and Flunisolide, both of which are indicated for Asthma. This suggests a potential pathway where Tranilast may influence the development or severity of asthma through its effects on rhinitis. The evidence is supported by the shared indication of these drugs with asthma, indicating a possible mechanism involving the treatment of respiratory conditions. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role of Tranilast in modulating inflammatory responses that contribute to asthma, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, reinforcing the likelihood of a relationship between Tranilast and asthma through its effects on rhinitis and its associated medications.",
